# Spec-Driven Development

Before implementing a public API change or changing library behavior:

1. Read or create `specs/<feature>/SPEC.md` with BDD acceptance criteria and out-of-scope items
2. Get spec approval before writing contracts or code
3. Write tests from the BDD scenarios before implementation
4. If implementation reveals a spec gap, update the spec first — do not silently change behavior

New features require all four phases. Refactors must keep existing specs green or update specs explicitly.
